From be47ba540e2d2a0f5034f5fbd191a94f3dae227e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gigi <42325924+g-cqd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:51:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: W^X emulation keeps pages that patch their own code,
 handles faults under the trap-flag emulation, forgets stale released pages
 and can log per page

A page that has seen a store from code on or next to it is never released for being busy (the NFS16
CPUID-builder stub runs thousands of times; wine-0009 released its page after ~2000 runs and the next
run crashed), a fault under the trap-flag emulation opens the page for one step like any other instead
of releasing it for good (the stub crashed once the debug-register thread was done), a released page
is evaluated again after any protection change (RWX->RX->RWX, RWX->RW->RWX) or a decommit, and
WINE_RWX_WX_LOG=<hexstart>-<hexend>|all logs protect/skip/release/first-stores per page.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c |   2 +-
 dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h  |   2 +-
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c       | 185 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 163 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

